# ouroboros#190: __loop_exit__ / __loop_iterations__ at module scope. The
# AOT emitted the VM's per-iteration step only for observed programs, so a
# plain loop never stored either name (undefined variable) and, after a
# stall exit, a later normal exit read the stale "stalled". Measured on
# the pin: a condition-false exit stores "normal"; a `break` stores
# nothing (the previous value stays); a stall stores "stalled" and resets
# the iteration count; `for` loops do not count. Emitted only when the
# program reads one of the names.
n is 0
loop while n < 3:
    n is n + 1
print of __loop_exit__
print of __loop_iterations__
m is 0
loop while m < 10:
    m is m + 1
    if m == 4:
        break
print of __loop_exit__
print of __loop_iterations__
for k in [1, 2]:
    m is k
print of __loop_exit__
print of __loop_iterations__
y is 0
loop while not converged:
    y is y + 1
print of __loop_exit__
p is 0
loop while p < 10:
    p is p + 1
    if p == 4:
        break
print of __loop_exit__
print of __loop_iterations__
q is 0
loop while q < 2:
    q is q + 1
print of __loop_exit__
print of __loop_iterations__
